From: Sun Yuechi <sunyuechi@iscas.ac.cn>
Subject: [PATCH] ceph-crash: fall back on a missing keyring too

https://github.com/ceph/ceph/pull/71853, two commits:

ceph: exit with ENOENT when connecting fails with it

  Like EACCES, so callers can tell a missing keyring from other failures.

ceph-crash: fall back on a missing keyring too

  Since 3a0f9ee5099 post_crash() only tries the next auth name on EACCES,
  but a name without a keyring fails with ENOENT. A host without a
  client.crash.<hostname> key stopped there and posted nothing.

Signed-off-by: Sun Yuechi <sunyuechi@iscas.ac.cn>
---
  src/ceph-crash.in | 2 +-
  src/ceph.in       | 3 +++
  2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ceph-crash.in b/src/ceph-crash.in
index 25d7ca4..22c2d17 100644
--- a/src/ceph-crash.in
+++ b/src/ceph-crash.in
@@ -59,7 +59,7 @@ def post_crash(path):
         f.close()
         if rc == 0 and stderr == "":
             break
-        if rc == errno.EACCES:
+        if rc in (errno.EACCES, errno.ENOENT):
             log.debug('post %s as %s failed: %s' % (path, n, stderr))
         else:
             log.warning('post %s as %s failed: %s' % (path, n, stderr))
diff --git a/src/ceph.in b/src/ceph.in
index 8872556..d8f4fc0 100644
--- a/src/ceph.in
+++ b/src/ceph.in
@@ -1096,6 +1096,9 @@ def main():
     except rados.PermissionDeniedError as e:
         print(str(e), file=sys.stderr)
         return errno.EACCES
+    except rados.ObjectNotFound as e:
+        print(str(e), file=sys.stderr)
+        return errno.ENOENT
     except Exception as e:
         print(str(e), file=sys.stderr)
         return 1
